Checked against `direction/delivery-spec.md`, `shotlist.csv` (director e8e4d60 / direction-v3), `edit/timeline.json`, `design/characters.md`.
Method: downloaded the release mp4 (sha256 454490bb…9e49658, identical to editor `film/elephants-dream.mp4`); ffmpeg 7.0.2 decode, per-frame difference analysis of all 15800 frames, mid-frame of every shot (`evidence/cut-v3/midframes-0..6.jpg`), correlation of each shot against the original's frames (`shotan.py`/`shotan.json`). Not played in a browser, not listened to by a person.

**Recommendation: FIX, not lockable.** The cut is now complete (no slates) and passes the file, mix, length, subtitle and no-original-pixels checks. What decides it: F1 (shots in a scene run share one picture, so most shot-list shots are not shown), F2 (S002 ghost edge, open), F3 (six lines unclear, open) and the new F4 (stepped motion).

