## Passes (observed)
- D1: MP4 H.264 High yuv420p 1024x576 24 fps constant, 15800 frames, AAC-LC 48 kHz 194 kb/s, 10:58.33; full decode prints nothing.
- D4 mix: audio stream identical to cut-v2: −20.6 LUFS, max sample −1.5 dBFS, no clipping, no silence > 1.5 s, no original audio in the sampled windows (see report-cut-v2.md).
- D2: 126 picture shots + credits; every shot sits at its timeline frames (editor's frame test; I saw the shot changes at the expected frames in the difference trace). The S027/S056/S070 joins carry no cut (same picture continues).
- D3 no original pixels: every shot's mid-frame correlated with the original's frame at the same time (max 0.32) and against the original's frames every 0.25 s across the whole film (max 0.51; a copy or a filtered trace would be ≳ 0.9). Frame-by-frame SSIM for S002 gave 0.35–0.42 earlier. So I found no copy of original frames; that is a correlation test at 128x72 grey, not a proof against a stylised re-trace.
- D3 characters: Proog (bald, grey side hair, olive coat, dark red vest, long nose) and Emo (young, dark hair, grey/teal shirt) are recognisably the same in all ten scene runs and match `design/characters.md`; places keep their colour identities (teal machine hall, black cable space, red telephone room, green pipe balcony, sepia elevator, white-gold machine, green fan room, orange pipe hall, green tubed floor). No melted faces, extra limbs or garbled text seen in the mid-frames at 320x180; at this size I could not inspect hands closely.
- D3 variation vs original: pictures are new renderings in a different, more painterly style (original is Blender 3D); the design sheets, not the original's look, are the standard.
- D5: unchanged from cut-v2 (75 cues, starts = script, no overlaps).

